Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: A12 defaults to 60 Hz with the 60-hblank timing

The refresh_60hz mode added 19 vertical blanking lines (vtotal 664); on
the Powkiddy A12 that made the picture shake. Keep the native vertical
timing and add horizontal blanking instead (htotal 1395): 54 MHz /
(1395 x 645) = 60.015 Hz, the 60-hblank trial that removed the shaking.
Its remaining black lines were the bootloader LCDC QoS setting, fixed in
U-Boot since.

At 60 Hz every 60 fps game frame is shown exactly once, where the native
~85 Hz mode alternates one and two refreshes, and Olduvai HD presents
faster (TEST_LOG test 49). Make it the default; refresh_60hz=0 selects
the native mode.
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-a12.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-a12.c
@@ -12,9 +12,9 @@
 #include <drm/drm_panel.h>
 #include <linux/media-bus-format.h>
 
-static bool refresh_60hz;
+static bool refresh_60hz = true;
 module_param(refresh_60hz, bool, 0444);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(refresh_60hz, "Prefer experimental 60 Hz timing (default: native timing)");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(refresh_60hz, "Prefer the 60 Hz (60-hblank) timing; 0 selects the native ~85 Hz timing (default: 60 Hz)");
 
 struct a12_panel {
 	struct drm_panel panel;
@@ -84,11 +84,13 @@
 		.flags = DRM_MODE_FLAG_NHSYNC | DRM_MODE_FLAG_NVSYNC,
 		.type = DRM_MODE_TYPE_DRIVER | DRM_MODE_TYPE_PREFERRED,
 	};
-	/* 594 MHz / 11; panel acceptance still needs a revision A hardware test. */
+	/* 60-hblank: 54 MHz (GPLL 594 MHz / 11) with the native vertical timing
+	 * and 41 more horizontal blanking clocks, 60.015 Hz. The earlier
+	 * vtotal 664 variant made the panel shake (TEST_LOG 2026-10-10). */
 	static const struct drm_display_mode experimental = {
 		.clock = 54000,
-		.hdisplay = 1024, .hsync_start = 1184, .hsync_end = 1194, .htotal = 1354,
-		.vdisplay = 600, .vsync_start = 612, .vsync_end = 622, .vtotal = 664,
+		.hdisplay = 1024, .hsync_start = 1184, .hsync_end = 1194, .htotal = 1395,
+		.vdisplay = 600, .vsync_start = 612, .vsync_end = 622, .vtotal = 645,
 		.flags = DRM_MODE_FLAG_NHSYNC | DRM_MODE_FLAG_NVSYNC,
 		.type = DRM_MODE_TYPE_DRIVER | DRM_MODE_TYPE_PREFERRED,
 	};
